# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. Unanchored, git matches this
# case-insensitively on Windows and silently swallows every lowercase
# 'package/' directory in the plugin trees - which is where the .ini and .esp
# files the packaging stages actually live. That is how a backup ends up
# quietly missing 22 files.
/Package/

# The snapshots are a durability copy of third-party sources. Nothing in this
# file may exclude them, whatever the rule was written for.
!/snapshots/
!/snapshots/**

distrib/
distrib_debug/
distrib_releasedbg/

.idea/

new_addresses.txt

packaged/*

.zcode/

# 文件名含控制字符的垃圾文件(禁止再次加入)
*.garbage
[0-1]S@@*

# agent working memory (not part of the shipped tree)
.workbuddy/

# python bytecode from Tools/Scripts and Code/plugins/STRPM/tools
__pycache__/

# Scratch trees used to exercise the packaging scripts locally.
# They leaked into a commit once; listing them is cheaper than remembering.
.pv/
.rx/
.px/
mod-pack*/
dist-dryrun/

# The Papyrus compiler the compile script downloads and unpacks. A build
# input that is fetched, not committed: the script pins the release tag and
# verifies the archive hash.
.papyrus-tool/

# The compiler's own cache directory. It is created relative to the process
# working directory - not to any path it is given - so it appears at the
# repository root whenever a compile script runs from there, which is what
# Compile-ShippingScripts.ps1 and Compile-OStimConsentScripts.ps1 now do
# deliberately. Unignored, it shows up as an unexplained untracked directory
# after every local build.
/.papyrus/
